IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-seat`

-- Magna Carta (1215) -- WORKED CASES FOR THE SEAT.
-- One or more cases for every question in mc15-seat.l4, each a person stating facts and the answer
-- the text gives, and a case outside the text ("not covered") for every question that has one.
-- Every expected value was written from the text before the file was run, except the cases marked
-- `-- RECONCILED`, which were re-derived from the text and the rule after a first run, each comment quoting
-- the original (NOTES.md, "Where the text says no, and where it does not").  Nothing here says that
-- any provision was, or is, in force or applied.

§ `Magna Carta (1215) -- worked cases for the seat`

§§ `The liberties the Charter grants (chapter 1)`

-- Under chapter 1, do I hold the liberties this Charter grants?
-- A freeman.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 1, do I hold the liberties this Charter grants` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Entitled
-- The heir of a freeman.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 1, do I hold the liberties this Charter grants` FALSE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- Neither: the text does not say whether others hold them.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 1, do I hold the liberties this Charter grants` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

§§ `My inheritance, wardship and marriage (chapters 2 to 8)`

-- Under chapter 2, do I have my inheritance on paying the ancient relief?
-- A baron's heir of full age who has paid.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 2, do I have my inheritance on paying the ancient relief` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- The same heir before paying.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 2, do I have my inheritance on paying the ancient relief` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- The holder was neither an earl or baron nor a tenant in chief by military service.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 2, do I have my inheritance on paying the ancient relief` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

-- How much relief must I give?
-- An earl's barony, nothing less owed by custom.
#ASSERT `How much relief must I give` `a whole earl's barony` FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST (Pounds 100)
-- A barony where custom makes me owe 60.
#ASSERT `How much relief must I give` `a whole barony` TRUE 60 EQUALS JUST (Pounds 60)
-- A knight's fee where custom makes me owe 150: the Charter names 100s at most.
#ASSERT `How much relief must I give` `a whole knight's fee` TRUE 150 EQUALS JUST (Shillings 100)
-- A knight's fee with nothing owed by custom: the text names only a ceiling and states no sum.
#ASSERT `How much relief must I give` `a whole knight's fee` FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under chapter 3, may the King demand a relief or a fine from me when I come of age, having been a minor in wardship?
-- A baron's heir who came of age out of wardship.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 3, may the King demand a relief or a fine from me when I come of age, having been a minor in wardship` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- An heir who was not in wardship.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was (An heir who was not in wardship., NC); the sweep of 2026-10-30 found the text's own word on this branch, so the no.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 3, may the King demand a relief or a fine from me when I come of age, having been a minor in wardship` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`

-- Under chapter 4, may my guardian take this from my land?
-- Reasonable produce only.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 4, may my guardian take this from my land` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- More than is reasonable.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 4, may my guardian take this from my land` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- With waste of the men or goods.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 4, may my guardian take this from my land` FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred

-- What follows if my guardian lays waste?
-- Committed to the sheriff, waste made.
#ASSERT `What follows if my guardian lays waste` `committed by the King to the sheriff or another accountable to him` TRUE EQUALS `The King takes amends and the land is committed to two lawful and discreet men of that fee`
-- Given or sold to someone, waste made.
#ASSERT `What follows if my guardian lays waste` `given or sold by the King to someone` TRUE EQUALS `The wardship is lost and transferred to two lawful and discreet men of that fief`
-- No waste.
#ASSERT `What follows if my guardian lays waste` `given or sold by the King to someone` FALSE EQUALS `Nothing follows under chapter 4`

-- Under chapter 5, is the restoration of my land what the Charter requires?
-- All of it, stocked as the season requires.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 5, is the restoration of my land what the Charter requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Land restored but not stocked.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 5, is the restoration of my land what the Charter requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Under chapter 6, may I be married in this way?
-- No disparagement, kinsfolk told.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 6, may I be married in this way` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- A disparagement.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 6, may I be married in this way` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- Kinsfolk not told.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 6, may I be married in this way` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred

-- Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, be kept waiting or put to difficulty over my marriage portion and inheritance?
-- A widow.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, be kept waiting or put to difficulty over my marriage portion and inheritance` TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- Not yet a widow.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, be kept waiting or put to difficulty over my marriage portion and inheritance` FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, be made to give anything for my dower, my marriage portion or our inheritance?
-- Asked for something for her dower.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, be made to give anything for my dower, my marriage portion or our inheritance` TRUE `something for her dower` EQUALS Barred
-- Asked for some other payment.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, be made to give anything for my dower, my marriage portion or our inheritance` TRUE `some other payment` EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- Her husband is alive.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, be made to give anything for my dower, my marriage portion or our inheritance` FALSE `something for her dower` EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, remain in my husband's house?
-- Ten days after.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, remain in my husband's house` 10 EQUALS Entitled
-- The fortieth day.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, remain in my husband's house` 40 EQUALS Entitled
-- The forty-first day: the text is silent.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, remain in my husband's house` 41 EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

-- Under chapter 7, was my dower assigned within the forty days?
-- On the fortieth day.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 7, was my dower assigned within the forty days` 40 EQUALS TRUE
-- On the forty-first.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 7, was my dower assigned within the forty days` 41 EQUALS FALSE

-- Under chapter 8, may I, a widow, be compelled to marry?
-- A widow who prefers to live alone and gives security.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 8, may I, a widow, be compelled to marry` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- A widow who prefers to live alone and gives no security.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 8, may I, a widow, be compelled to marry` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- Not a widow.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 8, may I, a widow, be compelled to marry` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- Whose consent does my security against remarrying bind me to?
-- She holds of the King.
#ASSERT `Whose consent does my security against remarrying bind me to` TRUE EQUALS `the King's consent`
-- She holds of another lord.
#ASSERT `Whose consent does my security against remarrying bind me to` FALSE EQUALS `the consent of the lord of whom she holds`

§§ `Debts and sureties (chapters 9 to 11)`

-- Under chapter 9, may the King or his bailiffs seize my land or rent for my debt?
-- The King, my chattels suffice.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 9, may the King or his bailiffs seize my land or rent for my debt` `the King` TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- A bailiff, my chattels do not suffice.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 9, may the King or his bailiffs seize my land or rent for my debt` `a bailiff` FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- A sheriff: the text names the King and his bailiffs.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 9, may the King or his bailiffs seize my land or rent for my debt` `a sheriff` TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- Under chapter 9, may my sureties be distrained while I am able to pay?
-- I can pay.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 9, may my sureties be distrained while I am able to pay` TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- I cannot pay.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 9, may my sureties be distrained while I am able to pay` FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`

-- Under chapter 9, must I, as a surety, answer for the debt?
-- The debtor cannot pay and has failed.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 9, must I, as a surety, answer for the debt` FALSE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
-- The debtor can pay.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 9, must I, as a surety, answer for the debt` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not obliged`
-- The debtor cannot pay but has not yet failed.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was (The debtor cannot pay but has not yet failed., OC); the sweep of 2026-10-30 found the text's own word on this branch, so the no.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 9, must I, as a surety, answer for the debt` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not obliged`

-- Under chapter 9, may I, a surety who has paid, have the lands and rents of the debtor?
-- Paid, not indemnified, no proof of discharge.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 9, may I, a surety who has paid, have the lands and rents of the debtor` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS Entitled
-- Indemnified.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 9, may I, a surety who has paid, have the lands and rents of the debtor` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not entitled`
-- Proof of discharge shown.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 9, may I, a surety who has paid, have the lands and rents of the debtor` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`
-- Have not paid.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 9, may I, a surety who has paid, have the lands and rents of the debtor` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

-- Under chapter 10, may the debt I owe to the Jews bear interest while the heir is under age?
-- Borrower dead, heir under age.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 10, may the debt I owe to the Jews bear interest while the heir is under age` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- Borrower dead, heir of age.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 10, may the debt I owe to the Jews bear interest while the heir is under age` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- Not a loan from the Jews.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 10, may the debt I owe to the Jews bear interest while the heir is under age` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- Under chapter 10, may the King take more than the principal sum of a debt that has fallen into his hands?
-- The King would take more than the principal.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 10, may the King take more than the principal sum of a debt that has fallen into his hands` TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 150 EQUALS Barred
-- Exactly the principal.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 10, may the King take more than the principal sum of a debt that has fallen into his hands` TRUE TRUE TRUE 100 100 EQUALS `Not barred`
-- The debt has not fallen into his hands.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was (The debt has not fallen into his hands., NC); the sweep of 2026-10-30 found the text's own word on this branch, so the no.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 10, may the King take more than the principal sum of a debt that has fallen into his hands` TRUE TRUE FALSE 100 150 EQUALS `Not barred`

-- Under chapter 11, do I, as the widow, keep my dower and pay nothing of my husband's debt?
-- Debt to the Jews.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 11, do I, as the widow, keep my dower and pay nothing of my husband's debt` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- Debt to others.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 11, do I, as the widow, keep my dower and pay nothing of my husband's debt` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- No debt.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 11, do I, as the widow, keep my dower and pay nothing of my husband's debt` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

-- Under chapter 11, must necessaries be provided for my children under age?
-- A child under age, a debt to the Jews.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 11, must necessaries be provided for my children under age` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- No child under age.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was (No child under age., EC); the sweep of 2026-10-30 found the text's own word on this branch, so the no.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 11, must necessaries be provided for my children under age` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not entitled`

-- How much of the debt is paid out of what remains after the dower and the necessaries?
-- The residue is less than the debt.
#ASSERT `How much of the debt is paid out of what remains after the dower and the necessaries` 100 60 EQUALS 60
-- The residue covers the debt.
#ASSERT `How much of the debt is paid out of what remains after the dower and the necessaries` 100 150 EQUALS 100

§§ `Taxes and levies (chapters 12 to 16)`

-- Under chapter 12, may the King impose this scutage or aid on me?
-- A reasonable aid to ransom the King.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 12, may the King impose this scutage or aid on me` Aid `ransoming the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- An aid to ransom the King that is not reasonable.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 12, may the King impose this scutage or aid on me` Aid `ransoming the person` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- A second aid to marry the eldest daughter.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 12, may the King impose this scutage or aid on me` Aid `once marrying the eldest daughter` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- A scutage without common counsel.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 12, may the King impose this scutage or aid on me` Scutage `some other purpose` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred

-- Under chapter 12, may an aid be imposed on me, a citizen of London?
-- A reasonable aid to ransom the King.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 12, may an aid be imposed on me, a citizen of London` `ransoming the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- An aid for some other purpose without common counsel.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 12, may an aid be imposed on me, a citizen of London` `some other purpose` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred

-- Under chapter 13, do I, a citizen of London, keep my ancient liberties and free customs?
-- A citizen of London.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 13, do I, a citizen of London, keep my ancient liberties and free customs` TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- Not a citizen of London.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 13, do I, a citizen of London, keep my ancient liberties and free customs` FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

-- Under chapter 13, does my city, borough, town or port keep its liberties and free customs?
-- A borough.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 13, does my city, borough, town or port keep its liberties and free customs` TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- Not one of those named.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 13, does my city, borough, town or port keep its liberties and free customs` FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

-- Under chapter 14, was the summons for the common counsel made as the Charter requires?
-- Forty days' notice.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 14, was the summons for the common counsel made as the Charter requires` TRUE TRUE 40 TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Thirty-nine days' notice.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 14, was the summons for the common counsel made as the Charter requires` TRUE TRUE 39 TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- No place fixed.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 14, was the summons for the common counsel made as the Charter requires` TRUE TRUE 60 FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Under chapter 14, does the business proceed on the day appointed even if not all who were summoned have come?
-- Summons made properly, some absent.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 14, does the business proceed on the day appointed even if not all who were summoned have come` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
-- Summons not made properly.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 14, does the business proceed on the day appointed even if not all who were summoned have come` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`

-- Under chapter 15, may the King license my lord to take an aid from me?
-- To ransom the lord.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 15, may the King license my lord to take an aid from me` `ransoming the person` FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- A second aid for the eldest daughter's marriage.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 15, may the King license my lord to take an aid from me` `once marrying the eldest daughter` TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- For some other purpose.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 15, may the King license my lord to take an aid from me` `some other purpose` FALSE EQUALS Barred

-- Under chapter 15, may my lord take this aid from me?
-- A reasonable aid to ransom him.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 15, may my lord take this aid from me` `ransoming the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- An aid that is not reasonable.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 15, may my lord take this aid from me` `ransoming the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- For some other purpose: this chapter does not speak.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 15, may my lord take this aid from me` `some other purpose` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- Under chapter 16, may I be made to do greater service than is due from my holding?
-- More than is due.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 16, may I be made to do greater service than is due from my holding` TRUE 11 10 EQUALS Barred
-- Exactly what is due.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 16, may I be made to do greater service than is due from my holding` TRUE 10 10 EQUALS `Not barred`
-- Not a free tenement.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 16, may I be made to do greater service than is due from my holding` FALSE 11 10 EQUALS `Bar not covered`

§§ `Courts and justice (chapters 17 to 22)`

-- Under chapter 17, may my common plea be heard wherever the King's court happens to be?
-- A common plea held in a fixed place.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 17, may my common plea be heard wherever the King's court happens to be` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- A common plea following the court.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 17, may my common plea be heard wherever the King's court happens to be` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- Not a common plea.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 17, may my common plea be heard wherever the King's court happens to be` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- Under chapter 18, may my inquest be held here?
-- Novel disseisin, in the county court.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 18, may my inquest be held here` `novel disseisin` TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- Mort d'ancestor, elsewhere.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 18, may my inquest be held here` `mort d'ancestor` FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- Another kind of inquest.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 18, may my inquest be held here` `some other kind of inquest` FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- Under chapter 18, were the justiciars sent through my county often enough?
-- Four times.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 18, were the justiciars sent through my county often enough` 4 EQUALS TRUE
-- Three times.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 18, were the justiciars sent through my county often enough` 3 EQUALS FALSE

-- Under chapter 18, are the assizes held as the Charter requires?
-- Two justiciars, four knights chosen by the county.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 18, are the assizes held as the Charter requires` 2 4 TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Three knights.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 18, are the assizes held as the Charter requires` 2 3 TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- One justiciar.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 18, are the assizes held as the Charter requires` 1 4 TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- Under chapter 19, do enough of the knights and freeholders present remain?
-- As many as needed.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 19, do enough of the knights and freeholders present remain` 5 5 EQUALS TRUE
-- One fewer than needed.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 19, do enough of the knights and freeholders present remain` 4 5 EQUALS FALSE

-- Under chapter 19, must I, a knight or freeholder who was present at the county court, remain?
-- Assize cannot be taken, too few remain.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 19, must I, a knight or freeholder who was present at the county court, remain` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
-- Enough already remain.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 19, must I, a knight or freeholder who was present at the county court, remain` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- I was not present.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 19, must I, a knight or freeholder who was present at the county court, remain` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- Every assize can be taken on the day.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: new case; the same inputs were `Obligation not covered` before the text's own if ("And if any of the said assizes cannot be taken") was read as a no.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 19, must I, a knight or freeholder who was present at the county court, remain` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not obliged`

-- What is saved to me if I am amerced?
-- A freeman.
#ASSERT `What is saved to me if I am amerced` `a freeman` EQUALS `his contenement`
-- A merchant.
#ASSERT `What is saved to me if I am amerced` `a merchant` EQUALS `his wares`
-- A villein.
#ASSERT `What is saved to me if I am amerced` `a villein` EQUALS `his wainage`

-- Under chapter 20, may this amercement be imposed on me?
-- Proportionate, leaves what is saved, by honest men.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 20, may this amercement be imposed on me` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- Out of proportion to the offence.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 20, may this amercement be imposed on me` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- I have not fallen into the King's mercy.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was (I have not fallen into the King's mercy., NC); the sweep of 2026-10-30 found the text's own word on this branch, so the no.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 20, may this amercement be imposed on me` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`

-- Under chapter 21, may I, an earl or baron, be amerced in this way?
-- By his peers, proportionate.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 21, may I, an earl or baron, be amerced in this way` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- Not by his peers.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 21, may I, an earl or baron, be amerced in this way` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- Not an earl or baron.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 21, may I, an earl or baron, be amerced in this way` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- Under chapter 22, may I, a clerk, be amerced in this way?
-- In respect of his lay holding, after the manner of the others.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 22, may I, a clerk, be amerced in this way` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- Not after the manner of the others.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 22, may I, a clerk, be amerced in this way` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- Not a clerk.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 22, may I, a clerk, be amerced in this way` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

§§ `Exactions and the King's officers (chapters 23 to 32)`

-- Under chapter 23, may I be compelled to make a bridge at a river bank?
-- Bound from of old.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 23, may I be compelled to make a bridge at a river bank` TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- Not so bound.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 23, may I be compelled to make a bridge at a river bank` FALSE EQUALS Barred

-- Under chapter 24, may a sheriff, constable, coroner or bailiff hold pleas of the Crown?
-- A sheriff.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 24, may a sheriff, constable, coroner or bailiff hold pleas of the Crown` `a sheriff` EQUALS Barred
-- A coroner.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 24, may a sheriff, constable, coroner or bailiff hold pleas of the Crown` `a coroner` EQUALS Barred
-- The King: the chapter names only the officers.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 24, may a sheriff, constable, coroner or bailiff hold pleas of the Crown` `the King` EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- Under chapter 25, may this rent or payment be demanded of my county, hundred, wapentake or trithing?
-- A county asked 101 against an old rent of 100.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 25, may this rent or payment be demanded of my county, hundred, wapentake or trithing` `a county` 100 101 FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- A hundred asked the old rent.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 25, may this rent or payment be demanded of my county, hundred, wapentake or trithing` `a hundred` 50 50 FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- A demesne manor: excepted.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was (A demesne manor: excepted., NC); the sweep of 2026-10-30 found the text's own word on this branch, so the no.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 25, may this rent or payment be demanded of my county, hundred, wapentake or trithing` `a demesne manor` 100 200 TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`

-- Under chapter 26, may an officer attach and catalogue the chattels my deceased relative left, for a debt to the King?
-- A sheriff, to the value of the debt, with lawful men.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 26, may an officer attach and catalogue the chattels my deceased relative left, for a debt to the King` `a sheriff` TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 50 TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- More than the debt.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 26, may an officer attach and catalogue the chattels my deceased relative left, for a debt to the King` `a sheriff` TRUE TRUE TRUE 51 50 TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- A constable: not named.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 26, may an officer attach and catalogue the chattels my deceased relative left, for a debt to the King` `a constable` TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 50 TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- The sheriff has not exhibited letters patent.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: new case; the same inputs were `Entitlement not covered` before the text's own if ("our sheriff or bailiff shall exhibit our letters patent") was read as a no.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 26, may an officer attach and catalogue the chattels my deceased relative left, for a debt to the King` `a sheriff` TRUE FALSE TRUE 50 50 TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`

-- Under chapter 26, may the attached chattels be removed from the lay fief?
-- Attached, the debt unpaid.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 26, may the attached chattels be removed from the lay fief` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- Attached, the debt paid.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 26, may the attached chattels be removed from the lay fief` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- Nothing attached.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 26, may the attached chattels be removed from the lay fief` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- How much is left to the executors after the debt to the King?
-- Chattels 100, debt 60.
#ASSERT `How much is left to the executors after the debt to the King` 100 60 EQUALS 40
-- Debt larger than the chattels.
#ASSERT `How much is left to the executors after the debt to the King` 50 100 EQUALS 0

-- Under chapter 26, do my wife and children have their reasonable shares?
-- Nothing due, a wife and children.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 26, do my wife and children have their reasonable shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- A debt is due to the King.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was (A debt is due to the King., EC); the sweep of 2026-10-30 found the text's own word on this branch, so the no.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 26, do my wife and children have their reasonable shares` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`

-- How are the chattels of a freeman who died intestate distributed?
-- A freeman died intestate.
#ASSERT `How are the chattels of a freeman who died intestate distributed` TRUE EQUALS `By the hands of his nearest kinsfolk and friends, under the supervision of the church`
-- He left a will.
#ASSERT `How are the chattels of a freeman who died intestate distributed` FALSE EQUALS `Distribution not covered`

-- Under chapter 27, is the debt the deceased owed me saved to me?
-- Intestate, I was owed a debt.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 27, is the debt the deceased owed me saved to me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- I was owed nothing.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 27, is the debt the deceased owed me saved to me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

-- Under chapter 28, may a constable or bailiff take my corn or other provisions?
-- A constable, no money offered.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 28, may a constable or bailiff take my corn or other provisions` `a constable` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- A bailiff who pays at once.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 28, may a constable or bailiff take my corn or other provisions` `a bailiff` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- A sheriff: not named.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 28, may a constable or bailiff take my corn or other provisions` `a sheriff` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- Under chapter 29, may a constable compel me, a knight, to give money in lieu of castle-guard?
