-- By what law is a dispute over a tenement decided?
-- In England.
#ASSERT `By what law is a dispute over a tenement decided` `a tenement in England` EQUALS `the law of England`
-- In Wales.
#ASSERT `By what law is a dispute over a tenement decided` `a tenement in Wales` EQUALS `the law of Wales`
-- In the marches.
#ASSERT `By what law is a dispute over a tenement decided` `a tenement in the marches` EQUALS `the law of the marches`
-- Elsewhere.
#ASSERT `By what law is a dispute over a tenement decided` `a tenement elsewhere` EQUALS `Law not covered`

-- Under chapter 56, I am a Welshman: must I restore to the King and his men what I took without the judgment of their peers?
-- A Welshman who disseised without judgment.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 56, I am a Welshman: must I restore to the King and his men what I took without the judgment of their peers` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
-- Not a Welshman.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 56, I am a Welshman: must I restore to the King and his men what I took without the judgment of their peers` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`

-- Under chapter 57, I am a Welshman: does the King have respite for what his father or brother took from me?
-- Taken from a Welshman, still held.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 57, I am a Welshman: does the King have respite for what his father or brother took from me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS Entitled
-- The term has ended.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 57, I am a Welshman: does the King have respite for what his father or brother took from me` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`
-- Not taken by Henry or Richard.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 57, I am a Welshman: does the King have respite for what his father or brother took from me` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

-- Under chapter 57, I am a Welshman: must the King now grant full justice by the laws of the Welsh?
-- The King has returned.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 57, I am a Welshman: must the King now grant full justice by the laws of the Welsh` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
-- Not yet.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 57, I am a Welshman: must the King now grant full justice by the laws of the Welsh` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`

-- Under chapter 58, am I, the son of Llywelyn, a hostage of Wales, or a charter of the peace, to be given up?
-- The son of Llywelyn.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 58, am I, the son of Llywelyn, a hostage of Wales, or a charter of the peace, to be given up` `the son of Llywelyn` EQUALS Obliged
-- A hostage of Wales.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 58, am I, the son of Llywelyn, a hostage of Wales, or a charter of the peace, to be given up` `a hostage of Wales` EQUALS Obliged
-- Something else.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 58, am I, the son of Llywelyn, a hostage of Wales, or a charter of the peace, to be given up` `something else` EQUALS `Obligation not covered`

-- I am Alexander, King of Scots: how will the King deal with the return of my sisters and hostages, my franchises and my right?
-- No contrary charters.
#ASSERT `I am Alexander, King of Scots: how will the King deal with the return of my sisters and hostages, my franchises and my right` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `in the same manner as the King deals with his other barons of England`
-- The charters provide otherwise.
#ASSERT `I am Alexander, King of Scots: how will the King deal with the return of my sisters and hostages, my franchises and my right` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `as the charters held from William his father provide`
-- A different matter.
#ASSERT `I am Alexander, King of Scots: how will the King deal with the return of my sisters and hostages, my franchises and my right` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Treatment not covered`

-- Who judges the matter between the King of Scots and the King?
-- A matter of chapter 59.
#ASSERT `Who judges the matter between the King of Scots and the King` TRUE EQUALS `the judgment of his peers in the King's court`
-- A different matter.
#ASSERT `Who judges the matter between the King of Scots and the King` FALSE EQUALS `Forum not covered`

§§ `Observance, the security of the barons, remission and the enjoining clause (chapters 60 to 63)`

-- Under chapter 60, must I observe these customs and liberties towards my men?
-- A layman with men.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 60, must I observe these customs and liberties towards my men` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
-- With no men.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 60, must I observe these customs and liberties towards my men` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- Not of the kingdom.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 60, must I observe these customs and liberties towards my men` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`

-- To whom do the four barons repair with an offence against the peace?
-- The King is out of the realm.
#ASSERT `To whom do the four barons repair with an offence against the peace` TRUE EQUALS `the King's chief justiciar`
-- The King is in the realm.
#ASSERT `To whom do the four barons repair with an offence against the peace` FALSE EQUALS `the King`

-- By what day must the transgression be corrected?
-- Intimated on 15 January 2001.
#ASSERT `By what day must the transgression be corrected` 15 1 2001 EQUALS Date 24 2 2001
-- Intimated on 25 December 2001.
#ASSERT `By what day must the transgression be corrected` 25 12 2001 EQUALS Date 3 2 2002

-- Under chapter 61, must the four barons now refer the matter to the rest of the twenty-five?
-- The forty-first day, uncorrected.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, must the four barons now refer the matter to the rest of the twenty-five` 15 1 2001 25 2 2001 FALSE EQUALS Obliged
-- The fortieth day.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, must the four barons now refer the matter to the rest of the twenty-five` 15 1 2001 24 2 2001 FALSE EQUALS `Not obliged`
-- Corrected in time.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, must the four barons now refer the matter to the rest of the twenty-five` 15 1 2001 25 2 2001 TRUE EQUALS `Not obliged`

-- Under chapter 61, are the five-and-twenty barons to distrain and distress the King?
-- Referred, no redress.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, are the five-and-twenty barons to distrain and distress the King` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Obliged
-- Redress obtained.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, are the five-and-twenty barons to distrain and distress the King` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not obliged`
-- Not yet referred.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, are the five-and-twenty barons to distrain and distress the King` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`

-- Under chapter 61, may the person of the King, the queen or their children be harmed in the distraint?
-- The queen.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, may the person of the King, the queen or their children be harmed in the distraint` `the person of the queen` EQUALS Barred
-- Someone else.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, may the person of the King, the queen or their children be harmed in the distraint` `someone else` EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- Under chapter 61, do I have the King's leave to swear to obey the orders of the five-and-twenty barons?
-- I wish to swear.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, do I have the King's leave to swear to obey the orders of the five-and-twenty barons` TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- I do not.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, do I have the King's leave to swear to obey the orders of the five-and-twenty barons` FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

-- Under chapter 61, will the King compel me to swear to the twenty-five?
-- In the land and unwilling of my own accord.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, will the King compel me to swear to the twenty-five` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
-- Willing.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, will the King compel me to swear to the twenty-five` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`

-- Under chapter 61, is what those of the twenty-five who are present ordain held as fixed and established?
-- Thirteen of twenty-five.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, is what those of the twenty-five who are present ordain held as fixed and established` 25 13 EQUALS TRUE
-- A tie, ten of twenty.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, is what those of the twenty-five who are present ordain held as fixed and established` 20 10 EQUALS FALSE
-- One present, one for: the text sets no quorum.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 61, is what those of the twenty-five who are present ordain held as fixed and established` 1 1 EQUALS TRUE

-- What is the standing of a thing procured to revoke or diminish these concessions?
-- Procured to revoke a part.
#ASSERT `What is the standing of a thing procured to revoke or diminish these concessions` TRUE EQUALS `Void and null`
-- Not so procured.
#ASSERT `What is the standing of a thing procured to revoke or diminish these concessions` FALSE EQUALS `Validity not covered`

-- Under chapter 62, are the ill-will, hatreds and bitterness remitted and pardoned?
-- From the quarrel.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 62, are the ill-will, hatreds and bitterness remitted and pardoned` TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- Not from the quarrel.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 62, are the ill-will, hatreds and bitterness remitted and pardoned` FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

-- Under chapter 62, is my trespass remitted and forgiven?
-- Occasioned by the quarrel, within the period.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 62, is my trespass remitted and forgiven` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- Outside the period.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 62, is my trespass remitted and forgiven` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

-- Under chapter 63, do I and my heirs have and hold all the liberties, rights and concessions?
-- A man in the kingdom.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 63, do I and my heirs have and hold all the liberties, rights and concessions` TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- Not one.
#ASSERT `Under chapter 63, do I and my heirs have and hold all the liberties, rights and concessions` FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

-- assertions written: 331.  check.sh counts the assertions satisfied; the two must be equal.
